dakarp@amherst.edu writes:

>I am having trouble opening chests on PC nethack 3.0 j. When I try to apply a
>key on them, it says that there is no door there.  The same thing happens when
>I try the lockpick.  What should I be doing? -Dan

You need to be standing on a chest to open it.  When you apply the key
or lockpick, use the greater-than key ">" to signify the direction.
It has the same significance as the characters used for up and down
stairways.  Of course, there are a few other ways of opening a chest -
but those would be spoilers.
